Project Map Skill for Claude
============================

This Claude skill maps your full project (backend + frontend), tracks changes,
and generates a persistent project map (`project.map.md`) for Claude to reference.
It supports:
- C# backend (controllers, endpoints, DTOs)
- React frontend (pages, components, API calls)
- FE → BE mappings
- Automatic updates on project changes (with cooldown)
- Persistent context to avoid rescanning

Folder Structure
----------------
P2W (solution root)
├─ .claude
│   └─ skills
│       └─ project_map
│           ├─ project.map.md         ← auto-generated map file
│           ├─ map.rules.md           ← Claude rules for referencing the map
│           ├─ ai_map_updater.py      ← generates/upates the map
│           └─ map_watcher.py         ← watches project changes

Prerequisites
-------------
- Python 3.10+ installed
- pip (Python package manager)
- watchdog Python package (file system monitoring)
- Visual Studio / .NET installed for C# projects

Installation Steps
------------------

1. Install Python
- Download Python: https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/
- Check “Add Python to PATH” during installation
- Verify installation:
  > python --version

2. Install Watchdog
- Open PowerShell and run:
  > python -m pip install --upgrade pip
  > python -m pip install watchdog
- Verify installation:
  > python -m pip show watchdog

3. Place Project Map Skill
- Copy the folder `.claude/skills/project_map` into your project root.

4. Adjust Paths (Optional)
- By default, `map_watcher.py` uses:
  UPDATER = r"C:\Users\USER-PC\Desktop\P2W\.claude\skills\project_map\ai_map_updater.py"
- Update to match absolute path on the new project if different.
- Or keep relative paths if running from project root.

5. Start the Watcher
- From the project root:
  > python .claude\skills\project_map\map_watcher.py
- The watcher generates an initial map immediately.
- Subsequent updates occur at most once every 5 minutes (cooldown).

6. Configure Claude Rules
- Create or update `.claude/rules.md` with:
  System: Always consult `.claude/skills/project_map/project.map.md` before making any decisions. Do not rescan the project. Do not assume missing endpoints or components — only use information from the map.

- Also include:
  # Project Map Usage Rules
  1. Treat `project.map.md` as persistent memory of project structure.
  2. Update internal understanding only when the CHANGE LOG timestamp changes.
  3. Never modify `project.map.md`.
  4. Prioritize information from `project.map.md` over guesses.

How It Works
------------
1. Watcher (`map_watcher.py`) monitors your backend/frontend folders.
2. On first run or structural changes, Updater (`ai_map_updater.py`) generates `project.map.md`.
3. Claude reads `project.map.md` for persistent project knowledge.
4. Map includes:
   - Backend controllers & endpoints
   - DTO classes
   - Frontend pages, components, API calls
   - FE → BE mappings
   - Timestamped change log
5. The watcher never modifies code, only updates the map.

Tips
----
- Keep `project.map.md` inside `.claude/skills/project_map` for consistency.
- Adjust `IGNORE` folders in watcher/updater for your project structure.
- Use absolute path in watcher for reliability, or relative path if running from project root.
- Change `COOLDOWN` in `map_watcher.py` to adjust update frequency.

Summary
-------
- Place `.claude/skills/project_map` in project root
- Install Python + Watchdog
- Start watcher → initial map generated
- Claude reads `project.map.md` → persistent memory
- Updates automatically when project changes

